From 6a6db144d96352967623f38692dfc4b4fb814518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:10:38 +0100
Subject: wifi: mac80211: mesh: don't linearize SKBs unnecessarily
Git-commit: 6a6db144d96352967623f38692dfc4b4fb814518
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc3
References: git-fixes

If mesh fast-xmit cannot be used due to aggregation not
being fully set up yet, there's no need to linearize the
SKB. Avoid that, which addresses a stale pointer issue
in the caller.

Change-id: I6b93e6c7587faf8749f8366ed574ee2b79fd47a5
Fixes: 8b0f5cb6bc7c ("wifi: mac80211: use mesh header cache to speed up mesh forwarding")
Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 net/mac80211/rx.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/mac80211/rx.c b/net/mac80211/rx.c
index ecee9348c70d..be41dd7c53e8 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rx.c
@@ -2905,9 +2905,6 @@ ieee80211_rx_mesh_fast_forward(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 	if (!sta)
 		return false;
 
-	if (skb_linearize(skb))
-		return false;
-
 	tid = skb->priority & IEEE80211_QOS_CTL_TAG1D_MASK;
 	tid_tx = rcu_dereference(sta->ampdu_mlme.tid_tx[tid]);
 	if (tid_tx) {
@@ -2918,6 +2915,10 @@ ieee80211_rx_mesh_fast_forward(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 			tid_tx->last_tx = jiffies;
 	}
 
+	/* this function must not fail after this */
+	if (skb_linearize(skb))
+		return false;
+
 	ieee80211_aggr_check(sdata, sta, skb);
 
 	if (ieee80211_get_8023_tunnel_proto(skb->data + hdrlen,
-- 
